# Regex replace case-insensitive global

Verifies the `i` flag makes the pattern match regardless of case, so a single
`/hello/gi` rewrite normalizes the mixed-case words in `Hello HELLO hello`
to `hi hi hi`.

>>> source
const greeting: string = "Hello HELLO hello"->replace(/hello/gi, "hi")
print(greeting)

<<< stdout
hi hi hi

<<< stderr
